Coffee tables deserve better than being treated as glorified coasters. This month, three art books have arrived that you’d be terrified of staining with a beverage. They might actually get people to pick them up, flip through the pages and—imagine this—read something.

New York-raised New Delhi resident Peter D’Ascoli (@peterdascoli) brings four decades of India-inspired discoveries to the page; actor-editor Sudhanva Deshpande gets up-close with Goa-based Orijit Sen’s (orijitzen) childhood drawings, sketchbooks, and political memes; and photographer Adil Hasan’s (@tombomb_adil) shiny copy of 'Static' looks at our strange screen-filled lives. Consider them a Diwali gift for someone else or an excuse to upgrade your own bookshelf.

@sheyakurian at the link in bio.

