@sanyamalhotra_ in the ‘India Mini Ananas’ Set. 

As seen at India Couture Week ’26, the ‘India Mini Ananas’ set features a fully embellished mini skirt, intricately hand-embroidered with dori and sitara work. Paired with a matching bralette, the set is layered beneath a long jacket crafted in striped tissue. The lapel features a hand-embroidered signature ‘Pineapple’ motif patch, highlighting the transition between the striped tissue and silk velvet.

Discover the ‘India Mini Ananas’ set at House of Masaba stores or online (link in bio).

A sharply tailored black bandhgala crafted in pure wool suiting, detailed with intricate spring cord embroidery. The clean, structured silhouette provides a refined foundation for the dimensional embroidery, allowing the cord work to introduce texture and subtle ornament without disrupting the precision of the tailoring.

In Moonlit Palace, traditional surface craftsmanship is brought into dialogue with contemporary Indian tailoring. Spring cord embroidery transforms the classic bandhgala through texture and detail, allowing an established silhouette to take on a more tactile and contemporary expression.

